      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your perspective is well-supported by analyses of the Sahel and North Africa, where the lack of a unified state has indeed fueled extremist groups. From a purely strategic and long-term regional stability standpoint, the chaos that followed the intervention heavily suggests a failure in state-building and power resolution. While the immediate humanitarian goals were met, the resulting institutional collapse arguably created a more volatile and dangerous geopolitical environment in the long run.",
